(R) is running."]}, "overview": "Western Michigan's 4th District sits in a rare moment of genuine competition. Bill Huizenga, a Republican incumbent in a seat with a three-point Republican lean, faces state Senator Sean McCann in a race raters split between tossup and narrow leans on either side. The national midterm environment favors Democrats, and McCann has more cash on hand while outside groups have spent heavily against Huizenga, who has drawn criticism for skipping town halls and for rising gas prices on his watch.\n\nPrediction markets give McCann roughly a 57 to 58 percent chance, and several raters call the seat a Democratic flip opportunity. The main counterweight is the most recent independent poll, which shows Huizenga ahead by three among likely voters, and a conservative super PAC is promoting the Green Party candidate in a bid to split progressive votes. The forecast lands on a narrow McCann edge with wide uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5309, "margin": 0.42}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4667, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4711, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.4732, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4842, "margin": 0.3}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4178, "margin": -0.7}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4942, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.4707, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.417, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4657, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.5306, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.4314, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.5595, "margin": 0.4}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.4501, "margin": -0.3}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.5027, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.4045, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.4996, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.4991, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-